ass.","timestamp":1793162627999304687}],"created_at":1788805295821955237,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix artifacts exist only because a cutover once needed a bar to clear. `src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/discovery_shadow.py` (389 LOC, \"RP-06 S7 cross-gate discovery SHADOW comparator\") has zero src importers; its only consumer is `tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py`. `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py` (492 LOC, epic-c81c spot evals) has no CLI, Make or CI dispatch, so `main()` `:407` is unreachable; its pure helpers `_verdict_decision` `:79` and `_majority_decision` `:127` are imported by `provider_parity.py:52-57` and must be relocated. `code_review/workflow_ops.py:774 shadow_compare` is called only from tests. `workflow/gate_dispatch.py:38-41` re-exports `_attach_code_review_metrics` (canonical home `finalize.py:171`) solely for `tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py`. `workflow/lint_refs.py:35,730` passes through `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` (canonical home `lint_expr.py:41`); the other three names there are used and stay. ADR 0111 `:38-56` forbids internal-only shims. `tests/unit/workflow/test_legacy_helper_retirement_09f6.py` is a string-absence tombstone; ADR 0111 `:108-112` and ADR 0116 `:15,40` reject tombstoning, so it goes. `llm/parity.py` STAYS (`provider_parity.py:45,48` import it); only its `:1` docstring naming LangGraph is residue.\n\n**Every citation was re-measured on origin/main 339c0b3af7b, and each deleted symbol's references enumerated tree-wide, not sampled.** That corrected two counts: **12** `gate_dispatch._attach_code_review_metrics` call sites, not 11, and `shadow_compare` called from **two** tests, not three scattered lines.\n\n## Approach\n1. `git rm src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/discovery_shadow.py tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py`. In `docs/review-kernel.md` delete the `APPROVED_DELTAS` sentence ending `:200` and the \"**The shadow comparator**\" paragraph `:202`; the heading `:182`, sensitive-data paragraph `:211` and cache note `:223` also describe the discovery journal, so reword rather than delete.\n2. Move `_verdict_decision`/`_majority_decision` into `parity.py` as public `verdict_decision`/`majority_decision` (the names `provider_parity.py:53,56` already alias them to). Replace `provider_parity.py:48-57` with `from rebar.llm.parity import ItemRecord, majority_decision, verdict_decision` — absorbing the `ItemRecord` import `:48`, blank `:49`, the justifying comment `:50-51`, and both aliased blocks `:52-57`. Lines `:44-47` untouched. **Also rewrite the module docstring `:9` and `:11`**, which name `fidelity_spot_eval` and both underscore helpers; leaving them fails AC1. Then `git rm src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/fidelity_spot_eval_results.json tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py`. Rewrite `parity.py:1-4` to describe the non-inferiority bar `provider_parity` scores against. Edit `container_stage.py:80`, `docs/config.md:413` (drop the `main()` allowlist clause), `eval_specs/README.plan-review.md:86,101-102`.\n3. Delete both `shadow_compare` tests from `tests/unit/test_code_review_discovery.py` — `:246-255` and `:258-268`, plus separating blanks `:256-257`, `:269-270`. The AC2 comment `:271` and test `:272` are unrelated and STAY. Then delete `shadow_compare` from `workflow_ops.py:774` to the end of that function.\n4. `gate_dispatch.py`: drop `_attach_code_review_metrics` from the `:38-41` import (keep `CODE_REVIEW_STEP_IDS`, used `:443`), delete the `:36` comment and `:289` marker. In `test_code_review_fp_ledger.py` add `from rebar.llm.code_review.finalize import _attach_code_review_metrics` and rewrite all **12** calls at `:188,204,218,233,252,270,292,328,344,379,395,419`.\n5. `lint_refs.py`: drop `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` from the `:35` import and `__all__` `:730`. `lint.py:27` keeps the rest from `.lint_refs` and takes that name from `.lint_expr` (`:128` consumes it unchanged)