eping the `jira_dc_capability_map.py` assertion. **It cannot be repointed at another real file: `fidelity_spot_eval.py:101` is the tree's ONLY computed-mode consumer**, which is what that assertion guards. **Measured impact on the `:189` floor `assert len(files) >= 10`:** the census is **11** today; removing one leaves **10**, so the guard still passes, with zero margin. Keep the floor at 10 — it stays a valid \"narrowed or zero-match census\" guard, and lowering it would weaken the only protection that census has.\n`tests/unit/test_parity_bar.py:248`: retarget the docstring reference; add `test_verdict_decision_and_majority_decision` (FAIL gives block, findings give block, PASS gives advisory, tie gives block).\n`.github/complexity-baseline.json` is unaffected; deleted symbols bucket `stale`.\nRe-run the tree-wide per-symbol sweep before trusting the greps below.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"discovery_shadow\\|fidelity_spot_eval\\|shadow_compare\\|_attach_code_review_metrics\" -- src docs` returns EXACTLY three hits: `finalize.py:171` (definition), `finalize.py:330` (its one call site), and the comment `batch_runner.py:157`. All three name the CANONICAL symbol this story keeps.\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS\" -- src tests` shows no hit in `lint_refs.py`.\n- [ ] Every surviving `ENGINE_INJECTED_INPUTS` importer resolves to `lint_expr`.\n- [ ] `python -c \"from rebar.llm.evals import provider_parity; print(provider_parity.verdict_decision({'verdict':'FAIL'}))\"` prints `block`.\n- [ ] `git ls-files tests/unit/workflow/test_legacy_helper_retirement_09f6.py tests/unit/test_review_discovery_shadow.py tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_prerequisites_continuation_heldout.py` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git grep -c \"gate_dispatch._attach_code_review_metrics\" -- tests` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py` passes.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_rp01_s5_authoritative_oracle.py` passes, with `